>What exactly are bones levels, bones files, etc?

When you die (below level 3, and excluding some special levels), there
is a chance (1/3, I think) that, instead of vanishing entirely, you will
instead become an undead monster, and all your equipment will be left
lying around (with a high probability of being cursed).

When another game (on the same machine) enters the level on which you
died, there is a chance (again 1/3, I think), that instead of getting a
normal randomly generated level, the new player will meet the old player
(as the hostile undead). This can be bad (whatever killed the old player
will still be around), but if you can get past that, the undead and any
pets the old player had, you can nick all their stuff. This is good :-)

Aside: there is a utility called Hearse which allows players to swap the
data files which contain the so-called "bones" data between machines.
This is mostly considered to add to the fun.

